   "source": [
    "### Objective 4: Data Visualization\n",
    "\n",
    "**Observation:** In this exercise, I created five different visualizations using Matplotlib and Seaborn. The bar chart was used to compare total sales by product, while the line chart illustrated variation in sales across records. The histogram helped examine the distribution of sales values. The scatter plot was used to explore the relationship between price and quantity sold, and the box plot helped identify the spread of sales and potential outliers.\n",
    "\n",
    "These visualizations make numerical data easier to understand and help communicate patterns effectively. Data visualization is an important part of Data Science because it supports exploratory data analysis and helps identify useful insights before further statistical analysis."
